On 2009-02-28, tenayatenaya@gmail.com <tenayatenaya@gmail.com> wrote:
> I do not know what other people's experience with L is on Sporkhack,
> but I've still found that it is easy enough to genocide all 4 even
> though it takes 2 scrolls instead of just 1.  Perhaps the scroll of
> genocide could be further changed:
> uncursed: genocides a type of monster (e.g. master mind flayer)
> blessed: genocides d2 from a selected class (e.g. "L")

Nah... that'd actually make the uncursed scroll more useful.

The _real_ deterrent to genocidal mania, IMHO, is the existence of the
summon nasties monster spell, combined with the fact that the nastiest
of the nasties aren't genocidable.  Of course, that's a delayed
punishment, and it may take some players a while to figure out that
genociding every monster they don't like may not be a good idea.

(Also, most monsters in nethack have some positive uses.  Mind flayers
are tasty and make excellent pets.  Purple L can drop athames.  It's
not much, but it's enough to make me think twice before genociding
them too soon -- and later on I may not care anyway, since by then I
can handle them.)

> Or, maybe to make it even harder ...
> uncursed scroll of genocide: genocides one random type of monster,
> where no-role is safe
> blessed scroll of genocide: genocides one random letter, where @ is
> not safe (muhahaha)

That'd work, yeah, and it'd be suitably nasty.  Of course, the real
effect would be that everybody would just stop using those scrolls,
since the odds of the random genocide actually hitting something
useful would be so small compared to the risk.

Anyway, the reason scrolls of genocide exist at all is to give less
experienced players the possibility to avoid certain monsters they
don't feel they can handle.  They're _supposed_ to make the game
easier, if used in moderation.  If you don't want that, you might as
well just remove them from the game.

(Disclaimer: I don't play Spork, though I might give it a try at some
point, and I obviously don't speak for Derek.  He's free to nerf or
not nerf genocide in his game any way he wants.)

